1
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:04,820
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:10,690
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,590
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:17,260
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,770 --> 00:00:21,570
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:29,450 --> 00:00:31,380
I told you this long ago...

7
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:34,080
You belong to me.

8
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:37,660
If you want to free
yourself from my control...

9
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,060
...then just as you did before...

10
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:41,520
Wrest yourself away with your blade!

11
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:31,190
Goodbye...

12
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:03,560
Feel no shame about shape

13
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,470
Weather changes their phrase

14
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:09,230
Even mother will show you another way

15
00:02:09,230 --> 00:02:11,610
So put your glasses on

16
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:13,690
Nothing will be wrong

17
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:15,900
There's no blame. There's no fame

18
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:17,740
It's up to you

19
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:21,370
The first words should be found

20
00:02:21,990 --> 00:02:24,990
Whatever holds you back

21
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:26,370
I...

22
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:27,500
...can...

23
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:29,670
I can get it off

24
00:02:29,670 --> 00:02:30,670
Tell me what...

25
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:31,670
Tell me what...

26
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:33,500
Tell me what you want

27
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:34,590
I don't know why...

28
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:35,590
Don't know why...

29
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:37,590
Don't know why you're afraid

30
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,760
Tell me what...

31
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:39,720
Tell me what...

32
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,390
Tell me what you'd say

33
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:42,720
I don't know why...

34
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:43,800
Don't know why...

35
00:02:43,890 --> 00:02:44,600
Too late...

36
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,220
It's too late

37
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:55,150
Sparks

38
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,840
They look brave enough.

39
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:26,600
So many plucky fellows have
gathered to fight in my tournament!

40
00:03:26,890 --> 00:03:30,640
My lord, the final match
will begin at any moment.

41
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:38,070
He is a mercenary named Valencia,
well-known as the Prince of Massacre.

42
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:40,280
It's been said that he slaughtered...

43
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:45,410
...over one hundred thirty Midland
soldiers during the hundred-year war.

44
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:58,000
I am quite sure that Valencia will win...

45
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,930
Who is he?

46
00:04:10,930 --> 00:04:12,560
Hey, what are you doing?

47
00:04:14,270 --> 00:04:15,560
Can't you tell?

48
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:16,560
I'm a challenger.

49
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:17,820
That's ridiculous!

50
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:19,570
I'm his rightful opponent!

51
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:24,820
Hey, don't be such a stiff.

52
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,200
It's supposed to be a festive event.

53
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:30,740
You look pretty formidable.

54
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:34,290
What do you say?
How about taking me on?

55
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:38,670
My lord...

56
00:04:40,210 --> 00:04:44,800
Very well, I'll allow it! It's a sideshow
before the final bout. Go on then!

57
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,180
Hey, now you're talking!

58
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:51,720
Even if this is
for entertainment, a duel is a duel.

59
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:53,600
I'll give no quarter!

60
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:55,390
I wouldn't have it any other way!

61
00:04:58,940 --> 00:04:59,980
Take your stance!

62
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,320
No need, come anytime.

63
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:03,940
Ridiculous!

64
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,900
Are you telling me
you won't even take your stance?

65
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:49,320
I-I-I yield...

66
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,200
Well, well!

67
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:51,830
That man did it!

68
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:02,670
Well done, well done.

69
00:06:04,630 --> 00:06:07,840
Now then, would you
be interested in serving me?

70
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:09,590
Needless to say, I'll pay you very well.

71
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:13,810
Thanks, but I'm not interested
in that sort of thing...

72
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,600
My lord...

73
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:19,850
What a shame...

74
00:06:19,850 --> 00:06:22,480
Not to put a man of his caliber to use...

75
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:42,290
Guts!

76
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,040
Guts!

77
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,590
Welcome back!

78
00:06:45,590 --> 00:06:46,340
Easy, easy.

79
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:48,220
I was worried about you...

80
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:50,720
...because you were gone when I woke up!

81
00:06:52,850 --> 00:06:56,350
But Grandpa Godot was right after all.

82
00:06:57,810 --> 00:07:00,390
He told me that you would
come back here for sure!

83
00:07:07,570 --> 00:07:10,200
Sorry, but I need you to fix this again.

84
00:07:11,410 --> 00:07:12,410
Really!

85
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:16,030
After sitting around
and doing nothing for a week...

86
00:07:16,030 --> 00:07:18,250
...you suddenly try your skill in a tournament.

87
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:21,580
I see...

88
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:25,670
You fought against
a very skilled man this time...

89
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,670
A sword doesn't lie.

90
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:33,430
This sword tells me everything
about both you and your opponent.

91
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,760
Oh, this poor sword of yours...

92
00:07:38,350 --> 00:07:42,140
It's wielded by a man
who's blind to his own destiny.

93
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:47,570
Let me fix the sword, please?

94
00:07:47,570 --> 00:07:49,900
When you're a little older, Erica.

95
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:13,220
My destiny...

96
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:15,430
My dream...

97
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:24,230
Does this sword embody my dream?

98
00:08:24,770 --> 00:08:26,190
Guts!

99
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,230
Here we go!

100
00:08:28,230 --> 00:08:29,070
Okay!

101
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:51,000
Guts!

102
00:09:02,470 --> 00:09:06,270
I guess it was too much
to deal with at once, after all!

103
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:07,650
Yeah, it was.

104
00:09:11,650 --> 00:09:13,280
This is no dream.

105
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:15,820
This has always been by my side.

106
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:19,320
That's right. It's a part of my body.

107
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:34,130
Through all the pain I could hardly endure...

108
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:36,800
All those moments
when I was sure of my death...

109
00:09:37,590 --> 00:09:39,640
I overcame them all
with this sword by my side.

110
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:47,890
Here's one!

111
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:55,530
Unforgettable memories...
Unforgettable people...

112
00:09:56,780 --> 00:10:00,700
I've sensed them all at sword point.

113
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:06,500
This sword is proof of my very existence.

114
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:14,250
Guts!

115
00:10:14,590 --> 00:10:15,670
Guts!

116
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:18,880
Ouch!

117
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:21,470
Come on, stay still!

118
00:10:21,470 --> 00:10:23,810
You are quite reckless.

119
00:10:38,450 --> 00:10:42,160
Godot, why did you become a swordsmith?

120
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:46,040
We've been a family
of swordsmiths for generations.

121
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,960
Do you like it?

122
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:50,540
I don't know.

123
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:51,710
You don't know?

124
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:54,880
Erica likes it because it's fun.

125
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:57,130
I want to be a swordsmith too!

126
00:10:57,130 --> 00:10:58,590
Hey, be careful.

127
00:11:00,930 --> 00:11:04,350
I've gripped steel
before even learning to walk.

128
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,930
I strike...

129
00:11:09,140 --> 00:11:11,230
...the iron lying before me...

130
00:11:12,270 --> 00:11:15,320
...without thinking
about whether I like it or not.

131
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:20,530
I've always strived to improve my
skill... To forge even better swords...

132
00:11:21,030 --> 00:11:23,780
But then before I knew it,
I became an old man.

133
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:29,830
Why do I continue striking iron?
The truth is I have no idea.

134
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:36,290
But... there is one
certain thing that I do like about it.

135
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:39,760
Sparks...

136
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,550
I like seeing the sparks...

137
00:11:43,510 --> 00:11:45,470
I'm absorbed by them.

138
00:11:45,470 --> 00:11:51,270
For a moment, I can feel as if
my life is sparking before my eyes.

139
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,250
Sparks...

140
00:12:11,290 --> 00:12:12,870
Am I also attracted...

141
00:12:13,330 --> 00:12:14,290
...to sparks?

142
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:17,420
Light cascading off swords...

143
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:18,550
Tiny sparks...

144
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:22,050
For as long as my opponents and I have lived...

145
00:12:23,130 --> 00:12:26,600
Our swords crash into our very being,
scattering tiny sparks of light...

146
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,770
These sparks are like life itself.

147
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:37,900
Guts, ready?

148
00:12:37,900 --> 00:12:38,650
Yeah!

149
00:12:58,040 --> 00:12:59,500
You did it!

150
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,170
Guts!

151
00:13:01,170 --> 00:13:03,010
Finally, you did it!

152
00:13:03,010 --> 00:13:06,380
At the end of the day,
there's nothing left for me but this.

153
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:14,850
I wield my sword...
not for anyone else, but for myself...

154
00:13:15,730 --> 00:13:20,190
To generate my own sparks,
even if it's for a fleeting moment.

155
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:49,850
Are you leaving?

156
00:13:49,850 --> 00:13:52,100
Yeah, thanks for your help.

157
00:13:52,890 --> 00:13:56,640
After being sheltered for nearly a year,
that's all you have to say to me?

158
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,860
Take care of yourself.

159
00:14:01,020 --> 00:14:03,320
Of course I will!
I don't need you to tell me.

160
00:14:05,570 --> 00:14:06,570
So long.

161
00:14:09,410 --> 00:14:09,990
Hey...

162
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:14,490
Don't get yourself killed.

163
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:25,260
Master Godot!

164
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:36,470
What's the idea, coming over
here so early in the morning?

165
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:40,310
Do I even have to explain?
I'm here to place an order!

166
00:14:40,310 --> 00:14:41,610
An order?

167
00:14:41,610 --> 00:14:45,610
I want you to make as many
swords as you can immediately.

168
00:14:45,610 --> 00:14:47,860
Of course,
I'll pay you handsomely for this.

169
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:48,780
What's going on?

170
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:50,530
Did war break out?

171
00:14:50,530 --> 00:14:51,950
No...

172
00:14:51,950 --> 00:14:53,240
We're hunting down bandits!

173
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:54,830
Hunting bandits?

174
00:14:55,330 --> 00:14:57,370
Those fugitives
we've been hearing about...

175
00:14:57,370 --> 00:15:00,000
They're hiding in
the mountains just over the border.

176
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:03,460
I need weapons so I can make
some easy money before it's too late.

177
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,250
Fugitives?

178
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:07,380
You haven't heard?

179
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:08,590
You neither, master?

180
00:15:09,170 --> 00:15:10,550
Well, no surprise.

181
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:13,850
You guys live like hermits
down here, after all!

182
00:15:13,850 --> 00:15:17,270
Who are they, these bandits on the run?

183
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,980
They were once members
of a mercenary band that led a revolt...

184
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:22,690
...in Windham about a year ago.

185
00:15:23,150 --> 00:15:24,480
A mercenary band?

186
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:28,690
Yes, I'm told that they are led
by a woman with incredible skills.

187
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,320
A woman?

188
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:35,490
I heard that they also made quite
an impact in the hundred-year war.

189
00:15:35,830 --> 00:15:39,120
I don't remember the name though...

190
00:15:39,450 --> 00:15:42,670
...probably the band
of something... Band of...

191
00:15:42,670 --> 00:15:43,250
Yes!

192
00:15:43,250 --> 00:15:44,330
The Band of the Hawk!

193
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:47,500
Wait, what did you just say?

194
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:48,420
Huh?

195
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:50,010
I'm asking you what you just said!

196
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:51,380
W-Well...

197
00:15:51,380 --> 00:15:55,220
I said the Band of the Hawk,
led by a woman named Casca.

198
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,160
We finally found them...

199
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,370
...the Band of the Hawk.

200
00:16:15,370 --> 00:16:18,280
Damn, they gave us a lot of trouble.

201
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:23,330
Stop complaining. Remember,
they're not going to live past this night!

202
00:16:23,870 --> 00:16:26,500
We'll make sure
they get a good night's sleep!

203
00:17:02,410 --> 00:17:05,710
Don't work too hard...
You won't be able to keep it up.

204
00:17:06,370 --> 00:17:07,290
Judeau...

205
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,960
I understand your feelings.

206
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:14,220
But you're essentially the leader
of the Band of the Hawk.

207
00:17:15,630 --> 00:17:18,550
Everyone's exhausted because
we've been on the run for so long.

208
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:21,310
At a time like this,
we can't have you collapsing too!

209
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:22,390
I know.

210
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,980
A moment ago,
I got a report from our comrades...

211
00:17:25,980 --> 00:17:27,350
...who infiltrated Windham.

212
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:31,440
According to their report, Griffith is
confined in an underground dungeon...

213
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:34,360
...located at the lowest
level of Windham Palace.

214
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:39,740
Some of them have heard a distant
voice from the depths of the prison...

215
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:42,790
It could be him screaming or moaning.

216
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:44,790
However...

217
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:48,540
...the voice has not been
heard within this month.

218
00:17:51,710 --> 00:17:53,250
Everyone is exhausted.

219
00:17:53,670 --> 00:17:56,930
We can't live on the run
much longer. We've got to hurry!

220
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:58,800
Believe in them.

221
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:01,760
You've got to believe in your comrades.

222
00:18:02,390 --> 00:18:05,980
We have no choice but to pool
our talents together, every one of us.

223
00:18:06,310 --> 00:18:07,310
Judeau...

224
00:18:08,140 --> 00:18:10,400
Anyways, you should
at least get some rest.

225
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:14,320
You can't organize our mission
to rescue Griffith if you are so tired...

226
00:18:15,690 --> 00:18:17,240
You are right...

227
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,910
You need to eat and rest.

228
00:18:19,660 --> 00:18:20,490
Yeah...

229
00:18:24,870 --> 00:18:25,540
Judeau...

230
00:18:28,210 --> 00:18:29,250
Thank you.

231
00:19:01,990 --> 00:19:03,490
How's Casca?

232
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:05,700
Taking a little rest.

233
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,410
She should.

234
00:19:07,410 --> 00:19:09,830
Lately, she hasn't slept at all.

235
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,960
I think she's been doing a fine job.

236
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:16,800
If she hadn't assumed leadership,
by now we'd all be...

237
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:20,430
You're right.
We might not have survived this far...

238
00:19:22,090 --> 00:19:24,350
We've survived,
but what good has that done us?

239
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:30,890
Even if we make it out alive and
try to start fresh in some country...

240
00:19:30,890 --> 00:19:32,730
It could never happen!

241
00:19:34,230 --> 00:19:38,780
First of all, without Griffith,
we're just sheep without a shepherd.

242
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:40,650
We can't accomplish a thing.

243
00:19:40,650 --> 00:19:42,110
What are you talking about?

244
00:19:42,110 --> 00:19:45,120
It's obvious we need him, but that's
why we're all trying to rescue him!

245
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:49,080
Can you prove that Griffith is even still alive?

246
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:55,250
Who knows. It might be over...

247
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:57,500
All over for him...

248
00:19:58,050 --> 00:20:00,420
Then why are you here, Corkus?

249
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:03,300
Why didn't you leave with the deserters?

250
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:11,890
Rickert...

251
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:15,860
I wish he was here for us...

252
00:20:24,070 --> 00:20:24,990
What is it?

253
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:34,080
Enemy raid!

254
00:20:40,710 --> 00:20:42,510
The enemy is in the north woods!

255
00:20:42,510 --> 00:20:44,800
Third company, fourth company, counterattack!

256
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:48,430
All others, get the injured on carriages
and ride to the southern quarter!

257
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:09,490
Casca!

258
00:21:10,950 --> 00:21:12,200
I have you!

259
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:30,220
Stay alert, Captain.

260
00:21:37,650 --> 00:21:38,730
Guts...

261
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

262
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

263
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

264
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

265
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

266
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

267
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

268
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

269
